The pathwise integration with respect to local time leads to the following generalization of It\^{o}'s formula:
\begin{thm}Let $F$ be a real valued function such that $F_{-}^{\prime}(x)$ exists and is of bounded $p$-variation with $1\leq p<\frac{2}{3-\alpha}$. Moreover, assume that for any $M>0$
\begin{equation}\label{condition}

  \dsup_{|x|\leq M}\left[\int_{|y|<1}^{}\frac{dy}{|y|^{\alpha +1}}\left|F(x+y)-F(x)-F_{-}^{\prime}(x)y\right|\right] <\infty.
\end{equation}
Then for $t\geq 0$ we have $\P$-almost surely
\begin{eqnarray}\label{Ito formula}\nonumber
    F(X_t)&=&F(X_0)+\dint_{0}^{t}F^{\prime}(X_{s-})dX_s -\dint F_{-}^{\prime}(x)d_xL^{x}_{t}\\
          &&+ \sum_{0<s\leq t}\{F(X_s)-F(X_{s-})-F_{-}^{\prime}(X_{s-})\Delta X_s\}.
\end{eqnarray}
